    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2UThF91LQrHDWWAJF3dXMZi)_\n\nexc draws empty spreadsheet rows below the data down to the end of the window. In `sp-collec-query-exc--draw` the sheet's row limit (`exc-calc-sheet-limit`, from the exc source) is now set per buffer to the notes plus the header plus one row, so the table ends with a single empty row for adding an entry.\n\nWrap and column width are not changed (column widths already come from `sp-collec-query-exc-column-widths`).\n\nNot run in Emacs (none in the container): whether exc reads the buffer-local value while drawing is based on reading its source, so please check it on screen.\n\nThe `#NNN` placeholders in the CHANGELOG and doc entries are replaced with this PR's number.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiBvN7MM96hTgFDoZmk)_",
